[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I validated both the data plane and control plane and found the fabric healthy. Data plane: end-to-end ICMP between the hosts is working with 0% loss and low RTTs (pc_0_0 -> pc_0_1 avg ~1.44 ms; pc_0_1 -> pc_0_0 avg ~0.81 ms). Control plane: all BGP adjacencies across the CLOS are Established. On the leaves, leaf_router_0_0 (AS 65200) and leaf_router_0_1 (AS 65201) each have two eBGP peers (the two spines) up and are exchanging prefixes (PfxRcd=1 per spine). On the spines, spine_router_0_0 (AS 65100) and spine_router_0_1 (AS 65101) have three neighbors up (both leaves plus the super-spine) and are receiving the expected leaf prefixes. The super_spine_router_0 (AS 65000) has both spine neighbors up and is receiving prefixes from each. These observations confirm routes to both 10.0.0.0/24 and 10.0.1.0/24 are present and propagated, matching the successful pings.

Mechanism: Because all BGP sessions are Established and exchanging prefixes, the FIBs have valid next-hops for host subnets, resulting in successful forwarding between PCs. Localization: No down sessions or interface issues were observed on any device or link.

Root cause: No current fault is present; the earlier outage is not reproducible.

Corrective fix: No restart is required. Recommend monitoring BGP neighbor stability; if the symptom recurs, capture “show ip bgp summary” on the affected leaf/spine at the time and, if needed, restart frr only on the device showing a down neighbor. 
=== END ===